Falsifies `device_tree_blob::verification::from_bytes_is_total`.

The defect: `from_bytes` drops its check that the buffer holds the `totalsize` the header
declares. The remaining check still refuses a size smaller than a header, so the function still
reads as validating the size; but a header that claims more bytes than the buffer holds then
reaches `&bytes[..total]` and panics, where it should be `Truncated`.

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `&bytes[..total]`, for any buffer whose header declares a
`totalsize` larger than the buffer.

diff --git a/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs b/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs
index e2cc7dc99..409a20591 100644
--- a/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs
@@ -251,3 +251,3 @@ impl<'a> DeviceTreeBlob<'a> {
         let total = be32(bytes, 4)? as usize;
-        if bytes.len() < total || total < HEADER_BYTES {
+        if total < HEADER_BYTES {
             return Err(Error::Truncated);
